fork() – Creates a child process.
exec() – Executes the Linux command in the child process.
wait() – Makes the parent wait for the child to finish.
getpid() – Returns the process ID.
getppid() – Returns the parent process ID.
uname -a → Shows Linux and kernel information.
lscpu → Shows CPU information.
lsblk → Shows storage device information.
ps → Shows running processes.
top → Shows real-time system activity.

CPU – The OS manages CPU time using processes and scheduling.
Memory – The OS provides virtual memory to each process.
Storage – The OS manages storage through files and directories.
I/O – The OS uses device drivers to communicate with hardware.
The OS acts as a bridge between applications and hardware.
